  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/he-a900.html",
  "prefLabel": "He-A 907.06 Scheduling Requirements",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "He-A 907.06 Scheduling Requirements. Program providers shall conduct sessions to ensure course completion on a timely basis for all clients, as follows:\n\n(a) Programs shall offer a course when there are at least 6 clients scheduled for a course; and\n\n(b) If a course cannot be scheduled for 3 months because the minimum number of clients has not been met, the program provider shall refer clients to another phase II provider.\n\nSource. #7058, eff 7-21-99; ss by #8902, INTERIM, eff 7-13-07, EXPIRED: 1-9-08\n\nNew. #9082, eff 1-30-08 (from He-A 907.05); amd by #9578, EMERGENCY RULE, eff 10-23-09, EXPIRES: 4-21-10",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/he-a900.html"
